    {
      "abstract": "This dataset contains processed numerical data supporting the study entitled “Multi-Objective Optimization of Bend–Twist Coupled Blades for Passive Load Alleviation in a Large Floating Wind Turbine.” The study investigates the passive load-alleviation performance of bend–twist coupled (BTC) blades for the IEA 15 MW VolturnUS-S floating wind turbine. Bend–twist coupling is introduced through modifications to the composite layup angles and blade pre-twist, and a multi-objective optimization framework combining OpenFAST simulations, Kriging surrogate models, and the NSGA-II algorithm is employed to identify improved blade designs. The deposited files contain selected processed data used for surrogate-model development, multi-objective optimization, and numerical verification. Depending on the corresponding file, the dataset includes blade design variables, statistical response quantities obtained from OpenFAST simulations, surrogate-model prediction and validation results, Pareto-optimal solutions, and numerical results for selected optimized blade configurations. The response quantities considered in the study include blade-root bending moments, blade-tip deformation, generator power, and other response metrics relevant to evaluating blade load alleviation and aerodynamic–structural performance. The original IEA 15 MW reference wind turbine and VolturnUS-S floating-platform models are publicly available through their respective official repositories. The present dataset provides the processed numerical data generated and used in the analyses reported in the associated manuscript rather than a complete copy of the original reference models or the full raw OpenFAST simulation files.",
